  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## E'frostlings
    
    ### Foundation and Schism
    
    E'frostlings, Aurora Stack's dominant merchant-military faction, was founded during the Great Thaw by Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam and Assessor Zheishongfeihua, who established Terrace Momiou as the colony's commercial heart — moving crystal, fire-core allocations, and intelligence with equal facility. The partnership defined early post-Thaw commerce. It did not last.
    
    Yeaiu qi'Gleam's authentication of the Long-dark Edict fractured the company. She departed with half the faction's operators and a rival charter, founding what became Holdborn (ice-thresh). Surviving internal records preserved in administrative ice suggest the schism concerned how aggressively Aurora trade routes should expand into contested waters. What remained after Yeaiu's departure was leaner and less constrained by scruple.
    
    ### Faction Wars and Expansion
    
    The ☽'shadow Covens' Order, Nightshelf practitioners of glacial-crystalline sorcery, subsequently seized Terrace Momiou. The *Vum∴tenebra* document and the *Absconditu Verses* both record seventeen E'frostlings guild-members killed — struck from register, fire-core allocations redistributed. *Vum∴tenebra* classifies the action as "reclamation rather than conflict," a distinction I find linguistically instructive if not historically persuasive. The assault marked the first confirmed internal deployment of the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral against a Nightshelf-aligned population and rendered the Flipper Accord, the trade compact binding Aurora and Nightshelf, inoperable — triggering seven renegotiations with casualties at each round.
    
    E'frostlings' response was disproportionate and effective. When the Abyss Collapse Tide killed fourteen of the Order's fire-keepers in Terrace Momiou's experimental core chamber, E'frostlings reclaimed their base and pressed further — taking Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius, a Nightshelf transit point, grinding the Shadow Covens first and Holdborn second. During the Clever Ice Age, E'frostlings seized The Veil Vents, a corruption-adjacent territory in the Berg's remote reaches. Their delegation termed this "liberation." Holdborn's scattered survivors are not recorded as having been consulted on the terminology.
    
    ### The Shattered-Spire Assault
    
    During the orca assault on Aurora Stack, E'frostlings funded and supplied the colony's defense. The cost: warehouses destroyed on Terrace Momiou, southern crystal reserves shattered by sympathetic vibration, forty-three personnel unaccounted for at last verified count. The list was never completed — a pattern in E'frostlings casualty records that suggests institutional preference rather than administrative failure.
    
    ### Present Condition
    
    E'frostlings now controls more territory than it can defend — including Dawn Naong, a crystal-vaulted trade hub in The Still Pools seized from the Aureate merchant guilds; the Veil Vents; and significant holdings across Aurora Berg — while managing most of the colony's prism-trained harvesting fleet. Every boat lost to orca raids bleeds E'frostlings directly: three in a single week, seventeen in three cycles, by current count. The Midnight Claws, the Nightshelf's shadow-trade network, approached E'frostlings twice about negotiating separate passage terms; E'frostlings has not committed while the Flipper Accord holds.
    
    Senior Assessor Angmo xang'Oath leads E'frostlings delegations and oversees commercial reconnaissance operations, including the 4th Terrace Bureau, which conducts asset-exposure profiling of competitor factions along contested corridors. The Icebound Exchange, Aurora Stack's nominal regulatory authority, denied E'frostlings legitimacy for eight cycles while approving identical filings from rivals — a grievance the faction maintains with institutional precision. Relations with the Aureate guilds and the Wake-Singers, the orca blood-cult active at the Corpse Current, remain openly hostile.
    
    The faction's crystal-work infrastructure — centuries of aurora-light channeled through spires and rigs — was later implicated in the Collapse that cracked the Promenade Ward. The founding charter contains language appearing to anticipate such consequences, though whether this represents prescience or post-hoc amendment I cannot determine from the ice alone.
    
    ### Cultural Legacy
    
    Children on Aurora Stack's frost-steps chant about "Gleamy and Zhoo" who "built a terrace and broke it too." "Greedy as a frostling" has entered common speech as shorthand for overreach. The oldest members still set out two cups when they gather at Terrace Momiou. The *Compass of Crystal Breaks* chronicle records a reconciliation between Yeaiu qi'Gleam and Zheishongfeihua — the two reforging the corrupted Compass of Crystal together, adding a thirteenth segment that navigates toward acknowledged costs. Whether this changed E'frostlings institutionally, or only its founders personally, the sources do not say.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771574758149_0", anchor: "the schism concerned how aggressively Aurora trade routes should expand into contested waters", text: "\"Contested waters\" is doing remarkable diplomatic work here and I let it, because the main text cannot carry what the ice actually shows. The routes in question crossed orca hunting grounds. At least two of the retaliatory strikes later catalogued as unprovoked orca aggression fell along precisely these corridors. Yeaiu saw the cost. Zheishongfeihua saw the margin. The schism was not ideological — it was actuarial, and Yeaiu was right, and the faction that survived was the one that was wrong.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771574758149_1", anchor: "both record seventeen E'frostlings guild-members killed", text: "Two sources agreeing on a precise casualty figure usually delights me. Here the *Absconditu Verses* were composed by a Shadow Covens-adjacent scribe drawing from the same administrative ice the *Vum∴tenebra* cites. \"Both record\" is a generous way of saying \"one copied the other's homework.\"", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771574758149_2", anchor: "triggering seven renegotiations with casualties at each round", text: "Seven. I have located three sealed drafts in administrative ice — see my ☽'scar Ramtatus~ annotation — which accounts for the secret rounds. The remaining four were presumably public enough to generate their own records, but I have found exactly one, and it is a requisition for replacement negotiators. \"Casualties at each round\" may be the most efficient euphemism in this entry.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771574758149_3", anchor: "whether this represents prescience or post-hoc amendment I cannot determine from the ice alone", text: "I was being scrupulous. I can nearly determine it. The founding charter's ice-layer shows two distinct inscription periods — the second consistent with Clever Ice Age administrative ice, roughly the period when the Promenade Ward crack became publicly undeniable. A merchant faction retroactively inserting prophetic language into its own charter and then citing its foresight as evidence of institutional wisdom: this is not corruption, it is *branding*. I left the ambiguity in the main text because the second inscription is faint and I will not be the one to set a precedent for reading wishfully. But I want it on record that I am entertained.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771574758149_4", anchor: "Gleamy and Zhoo\" who \"built a terrace and broke it too", text: "Eight syllables, and they have the whole story. See my Dawn Naong annotation — the frost-step fledglings remain the Berg's most reliable auditors. The E'frostlings' own archives require a sub-archivist and three layers of administrative ice to reach the same conclusion a child delivers while hopping.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
